  "composition_summary": "Preserved the volatile tail exactly (one user message, no invented assistant reply). Task is a single class-22 pure-logic draft, which the supported sink accepts (name/description/content). The draft is a target-interface authoring artifact: it reads raw candidate data with inputs.get() so missing and null stay distinct, validates integer type/bounds/bool-exclusion before classifying, and returns the requested invalid-result object for malformed data instead of raising. It assigns result on every path, uses no imports/host/IO, and carries no defaults or coercion. This is an unapproved draft; Q1/Q2 and host execution are still required. No compatibility/intent/settings changes were proposed.",
